            {
              "chatMessage": {
                "text": "🟡 SprocketsCompletionContributorTest:20: `turbolinks` loses its version constraint while `ckeditor` on the next line keeps one, so `testResolveGemAssetInLibDirectory` and `testResolveToMostAppropriateGemFile` now follow whatever `turbolinks` version gems-data holds. Today that is 1.1.1 on master and 1.3.1 on `hjwylde/draft/ruby-35347-gem-updates`, and both ship `lib/assets/javascripts/turbolinks.js.coffee`. A later major bump changes the asset name and breaks both assertions. Add an upper bound, like the `ckeditor` one.",
                "details": {
                  "className": "M2TextItemContent"
                },
                "author": {
                  "name": "RubyMine Workflow",
